// The exported C symbols of ONNX Runtime, one novo-lang declaration
// each.  There are two of them.
//
// ONNX Runtime does not expose its C API as symbols.  It exposes ONE
// symbol, `OrtGetApiBase`, which answers the address of a structure of
// two function pointers; the second of those, `GetApi`, answers the
// address of the `OrtApi` structure, which holds every other call the
// C API has — creating an environment, creating a session, building a
// tensor, running inference, releasing anything — as a FIELD.  None of
// them is a name the loader can resolve, so none of them can be an
// `@ffi` declaration.
//
// The second symbol, `OrtSessionOptionsAppendExecutionProvider_CPU`, is
// a plain C function in the CPU provider factory, and it is declared
// here because it is a symbol.  It takes an `OrtSessionOptions`, which
// is made by a field of the table, so nothing in this package can
// produce an argument for it.
//
// A pointer is an `Int` and zero is null.  Reading a function pointer
// out of the table is `ptr.read_word`; calling one is not something the
// novo-lang foreign function interface does.  The README says what a
// program that wants the runtime has to do instead.

// Get the address of the `OrtApiBase` structure.
//
// This is the only entry point ONNX Runtime promises as a symbol, and
// it never fails: the answer is the address of a structure the library
// owns and never releases.
//
// The structure is two eight-byte function pointers, in this order.
//
// | Offset | Field | What it is |
// | --- | --- | --- |
// | 0 | `GetApi` | takes a version number, answers the address of the `OrtApi` table, or 0 when the library is older than the version asked for |
// | 8 | `GetVersionString` | takes nothing, answers the address of a string such as `"1.17.3"` |
//
// Both are addresses of C functions, and neither is callable from
// novo-lang. Read them with `ptr.read_word` to see that the library
// loaded; to use them, see the README.
pub @ffi(library = "onnxruntime", symbol = "OrtGetApiBase")
fn ort_get_api_base() -> Int [ffi]

// Add the CPU execution provider to a set of session options.
//
// `options` is an `OrtSessionOptions`, and `use_arena` is 1 to let the
// provider keep an arena allocator or 0 to allocate each time.
// Answers 0 on success, and otherwise the address of an `OrtStatus`
// the caller must release through the table.
//
// This is the CPU provider factory's one exported symbol, declared in
// `cpu_provider_factory.h`.  It is here because it is a symbol; it is
// not usable on its own, because an `OrtSessionOptions` is made by
// `CreateSessionOptions`, which is a field of the `OrtApi` table.
pub @ffi(library = "onnxruntime", symbol = "OrtSessionOptionsAppendExecutionProvider_CPU")
fn ort_session_options_append_execution_provider_cpu(options: Int, use_arena: Int) -> Int [io, ffi]
